Every release is published to `{{ cdnURL }}`.

#### ES modules

Each service, helper and enum is its own module, so the browser downloads only what you import. A service is served under its name in kebab case{% if services['tablesDB'] is defined %}, such as `TablesDB` from `tables-db.js`{% endif %}{% if enum %}, and enums under `enums/`, such as `{{ enum.title|caseUcfirst }}` from `enums/{{ enum.title|caseKebab }}.js`{% endif %}. `index.js` re-exports everything, so importing it loads every service:

```html
<script type="module">
    import {{ '{' }} Client {{ '}' }} from '{{ cdnURL }}client.js';
    import {{ '{' }} Account {{ '}' }} from '{{ cdnURL }}account.js';
{% if enum %}
    import {{ '{' }} {{ enum.title|caseUcfirst }} {{ '}' }} from '{{ cdnURL }}enums/{{ enum.title|caseKebab }}.js';
{% endif %}
</script>
```

#### Script tag

Add the script before any code that uses the SDK. It exposes every export on the global `Appwrite` object:

```html
<script src="{{ cdnURL }}sdk.min.js"></script>
<script>
    const {{ '{' }} Client, Account {{ '}' }} = Appwrite;
</script>
```

{% if services['analytics'] is defined %}
#### Analytics tracker

`tracker.js` is a single self-contained file that configures itself from its own script tag, so a page needs no JavaScript to send pageviews, outbound links, scroll depth and engagement time:

```html
<script defer src="{{ cdnURL }}tracker.js"
        data-endpoint="{{ (spec | endpoint) }}"
        data-project="<PROJECT_ID>"
        data-property="<PROPERTY_ID>"></script>
```

Add `data-respect-dnt="false"` to track regardless of `navigator.doNotTrack`, or `data-track-downloads="true"` to also track file downloads. The tracker is published on `window.__{{ spec.info.title | caseLower }}Tracker` for custom events, and `{{ spec.info.title | caseUcfirst }}.startTracking()` wires up a second property by hand. To drive tracking from an ES module instead, import `Tracking` from `{{ cdnURL }}analytics-tracking.js`.

{% endif %}
#### Subresource integrity

`integrity.json` in the same directory maps each `.js` file to its `sha384-` hash. An `integrity` attribute checks only the file it is set on. `sdk.min.js` is a single file, so its hash as the `integrity` attribute, together with `crossorigin="anonymous"`, covers the whole SDK. ES modules import other modules and shared chunks, so supply their hashes through the `integrity` field of an import map to cover those too.

